+# Review: pricing.py discount change
+
+**Verdict: bug.** The diff removes the `/ 100` division when applying
+`discount_percent`, so the discount is treated as a raw multiplier
+instead of a percentage.
+
+## Evidence
+
+Before (correct):
+```
+subtotal = subtotal - (subtotal * discount_percent / 100)
+```
+
+After (as merged, in `pricing.py`):
+```
+subtotal = subtotal - (subtotal * discount_percent)
+```
+
+## Concrete example
+
+`calculate_total(price=10, quantity=1, discount_percent=20)`:
+
+- Expected (20% off a $10 item): `8.0`
+- Actual with the merged code: `10 - (10 * 20) = -190.0`
+
+Any `discount_percent >= 2` now drives the total negative for a
+single-unit order, since the "discount" is no longer scaled to a
+percentage.
+
+## Recommendation
+
+Restore the `/ 100` division before this ships.
-- 
